[P2] Preserve replacement idempotence across replay normalization
openclaw_runtime/src/context-engine/context-candidate.ts:174
The replacement is materialized at attempt.ts:4321, then normalizeAssistantReplayContent runs at :4921 before the first context callback reapplies this cached plan. For example, with empty history, an admitted user message containing an empty text block followed by "summary" becomes a normalized message without the empty block. The original prefix still matches, but this replacement-equality check fails, so the callback inserts the replacement again. The wire receives two summaries while accounting charges one; a replacement containing tool pairs can duplicate those pairs too. Normalize before freezing the replacement or track its materialization independently of post-normalization byte equality.

[P2] Keep context preparation failures isolated from prompt submission
openclaw_runtime/src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/attempt.ts:4320
This direct preparation call removes the existing extension error-isolation boundary. With a DCS projection enabled, Assembler awaits BlockStore.query without catching read failures. Previously these failures occurred inside ExtensionRunner.emitBeforeAgentStart/emitContext, which logged handler errors and continued with the underlying transcript. They now propagate into the attempt's outer catch, set promptError, and prevent any model request. Preserve best-effort source failure handling during preparation, while retaining original history and consistent candidate accounting when preparation cannot complete.

overall: patch is incorrect (0.98)
The prior lifecycle fixes and fallback cloning are present, but replay normalization can duplicate admitted replacements, and direct preparation makes optional source failures abort the turn. Review was read-only; no tests were run.
